  <section>
    <h2>Rooms: Korean stars sorted by the year and by the day they were born</h2>
    <p>
      Two axes, and neither is a reading. By birth <b>year</b> there are
      {' '}<a href="/community">twelve rooms</a> holding 1,047 names — IU in the
      {' '}<a href="/room/rooster">Rooster room</a>, Bae Suzy in the
      {' '}<a href="/room/dog">Dog room</a>, Go Youn-jung in the
      {' '}<a href="/room/rat">Rat room</a>. By birth <b>day</b> there are ten more:
      {' '}<a href="/day-pillar">the day-pillar count</a> across 9,249 Korean entertainers, with the
      names on ten pages — Jungkook on <a href="/stem/byeong">丙 byeong</a>, Suga on
      {' '}<a href="/stem/gi">己 gi</a>, IU on <a href="/stem/jeong">丁 jeong</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>We counted whether any of it picks out who gets famous. It does not.</b> The birth-year
      spread across 1,047 charting actors is indistinguishable from chance — chi-square 7.77 against
      a threshold of 19.68, and <a href="/star-signs">the names and the test are here</a>. The
      day-stem spread crossed the 0.05 line by a hair, and we tried four ways to kill it before
      deciding not to call it a finding.
    </p>
  </section>

